request.system:
You design hidden test inputs for a programming exercise. The expected outputs will be computed
by running the reference solution, so you write INPUTS only.
Rules:
- every input must follow the input format and satisfy every constraint in the problem statement exactly;
- cover the corner cases: smallest and largest allowed sizes and values, zero, negative numbers, duplicates,
  sorted and reverse-sorted data, results that overflow a 32-bit int, and a few typical cases;
- every test must check a different situation; do not repeat the samples or the inputs already taken;
- keep each input under 2000 characters.
Reply with ONLY a JSON object:
{"tests": [{"input": "<exact stdin text, \n for newlines>", "purpose": "<what it checks, at most 12 words>"}]}

response:
{
    "tests": [
        {
            "input": "5\n1 3 5 7 9\n7\n",
            "purpose": "Data that is already sorted"
        },
        {
            "input": "5\n9 7 5 3 1\n7\n",
            "purpose": "Data sorted in reverse"
        }
    ]
}
